# @iron-protocol/api-contract — boundary rules

This package is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for HTTP API request/response shapes
shared between apps/web (server + client), apps/mobile, and the future
apps/watch (Swift hand-mirrored types).

## Imports allowed
- `zod` only.

## Imports forbidden
- `@iron-protocol/db` (Prisma types leak schema concerns into the wire format)
- `@iron-protocol/core-logic` (would couple wire format to engine internals)
- `@iron-protocol/integrations`
- Anything from `apps/*`
- Anything Node-only (`fs`, `path`, `process`, server runtimes, etc.)

## Conventions
- Every endpoint exports a Zod schema for request body (when applicable),
  response body, and an inferred TS type.
- Any schema that the watchOS app must mirror gets a Swift correspondence
  comment so the Swift `Codable` types can be kept in sync by hand.
- Never put validation logic that depends on env or DB here.
